      8 
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ارتبّهُ</span></b> : see 1. ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تَرْتَبُّ الشَّعَرَ</span> [<i>She adjusts,</i> or
<i>arranges, and composes,</i> or <i>collects together, the
hair</i>], said of a woman, is from [<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">الرَّبُّ</span> signifying]
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">الإِصْلَاحُ</span> and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">الجَمْعُ</span>. (M.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b3-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">اُرْتُبَّ العِنَبُ</span> <i>The
grapes were cooked so as to become</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">رُبّ</span> [or <i>rob</i>],
<i>used to give a relish to bread.</i> (AHn, M.)

